    "instruction": "Create a dark-mode toggle that persists the user's choice in localStorage and applies it before paint (anti-flash script).",
    "output": "<style>\n  :root { --bg: #fff; --text: #0f172a; }\n  html.dark { --bg: #0f172a; --text: #f1f5f9; }\n  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 2rem; }\n  button { padding: .6rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid currentColor; background: transparent; color: inherit; cursor: pointer; }\n</style>\n<script>\n  (function () {\n    const saved = localStorage.getItem('theme');\n    if (saved === 'dark' || (!saved && matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches)) {\n      document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');\n    }\n  })();\n  function toggleTheme() {\n    document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark');\n    localStorage.setItem('theme', document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark') ? 'dark' : 'light');\n  }\n</script>\n<body>\n  <button onclick=\"toggleTheme()\">Toggle theme</button>\n  <p>Choice persists across reloads without a flash of wrong colors.</p>\n</body>"
